# Authentication and security — Pulse

**Methodology:** [`docs/meta/ai_first_project_methodology.md`](docs/meta/ai_first_project_methodology.md)  
**Guide:** [`docs/guidelines/auth/ai_auth_implementation_guide.md`](docs/guidelines/auth/ai_auth_implementation_guide.md)  
**Schema:** [`docs/prds/03_data_model/database_schema_v1.md`](docs/prds/03_data_model/database_schema_v1.md)  
**Runtime:** [ADR-002](docs/prds/07_governance/adr_002_next162_vercel_runtime_policy.md) — Next.js **16.2.6**, **`proxy.ts`**

## Next.js 16 interception (not middleware-first)

- **Layer 1:** **`proxy.ts`** — JWT role gate via **`auth.config.ts`** (no Prisma, no full `auth.ts`)
- **`middleware.ts`:** legacy/transitional only — do not implement new auth gates here
- **Layer 2:** optional layout UX redirects
- **Layer 3:** mandatory `auth()` in Route Handlers and Server Actions
- **Layer 4:** `@{{PACKAGE_SCOPE}}/policy-server` object-level authorization

Split Auth.js config is **mandatory**: `auth.config.ts` for proxy; `auth.ts` (+ PrismaAdapter) for server `auth()` only.

## MVP auth model

- Credentials (email + password); `passwordHash` on `User`
- Role (`client` | `trainer` | `admin`) in JWT + session
- Password reset via `password_reset_token` + Resend

## Session typing

- Auth.js module augmentation — **only in `apps/web`**
- Map session → `PolicySessionContext` before policy-server
- See [typescript-monorepo-types.mdc](typescript-monorepo-types.mdc)

## Checklist

- [ ] Route protection in **`proxy.ts`**, not new `middleware.ts` logic
- [ ] Session verified on every mutation and protected read
- [ ] No `@{{PACKAGE_SCOPE}}/policy-server` in proxy/middleware

Reference: Pulse (docs/examples/pulse) `auth-security.mdc` — adapted for Pulse ADR-002.
